# Title: Feedback Loop
# Description: A multi-stage signal network in which later stages depend on earlier
# ones - including on their PREVIOUS value - i.e. feedback over time.
# The whole network is expressed as a single specification. Since the primary stage
# is o1[t] = i1[t], every look-back can be traced directly to the input i1, so no
# intermediate files are needed. Naming: primary=o1, secondary=o2, ifeedback=o3,
# feedback=o4, final=o5.
#
# Timing note: as soon as a specification contains a look-back [t-1], step 0 is an
# initialization step (there is no past yet) - all outputs are 0 there. The actual
# logic takes effect from step 1 onwards.

# === INPUT ===
i1 : sbf := in file("io/sequence.in")   # input signal (a bit sequence, one bit per line)

# === OUTPUTS (all to io/) ===
o1 : sbf := out file("io/primary.out")     # primary   = input directly
o2 : sbf := out file("io/secondary.out")   # secondary = negation of the PREVIOUS primary
o3 : sbf := out file("io/ifeedback.out")   # ifeedback = input AND secondary
o4 : sbf := out file("io/feedback.out")    # feedback  = feedback through ifeedback[t-1]
o5 : sbf := out file("io/final.out")       # final     = combination of the stages

# === THE NETWORK AS ONE SPEC ===
# Look-backs are resolved to the input i1 (o1[t]=i1[t], so o1[t-1]=i1[t-1], etc.):
#   secondary o2[t] = NOT primary[t-1]              = i1[t-1]'
#   ifeedback o3[t] = i1[t] AND secondary[t]        = i1[t] & i1[t-1]'
#   feedback  o4[t] = (ifeedback[t-1] XOR primary[t]) AND secondary[t]
#                                                   = ((i1[t-1] & i1[t-2]') ^ i1[t]) & i1[t-1]'
#   final     o5[t] = (o1&o2) | (o2&o3) | (o3&o1')  -> simplifies to i1[t] & i1[t-1]'
run always (
  (o1[t] = i1[t]) &&
  (o2[t] = i1[t-1]') &&
  (o3[t] = i1[t] & i1[t-1]') &&
  (o4[t] = ((i1[t-1] & i1[t-2]') ^ i1[t]) & i1[t-1]') &&
  (o5[t] = i1[t] & i1[t-1]')
)

# Example: io/sequence.in = 1,1,0,0,1  (step 0 = init = 0, then):
#   primary   o1 = _,1,0,0,1
#   secondary o2 = _,0,0,1,1
#   ifeedback o3 = _,0,0,0,1
#   feedback  o4 = _,0,0,0,1
#   final     o5 = _,0,0,0,1
